                        "sense_id": "42d30915-2fd0-30a6-ae46-0e65d9260863",
                        "entry_id": "dc58aa9a-5d43-348f-a473-920a564e27de",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An escribed circle; a circle outside a polygon (especially a triangle, but also sometimes a quadrilateral) that is tangent to each of the lines on which the sides of the polygon lie."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "573479c9-2498-494e-876e-d97f0404247b",
                                "sense_id": "42d30915-2fd0-30a6-ae46-0e65d9260863",
                                "text": "Also since the circle of inversion cuts both excircles orthogonally, each excircle inverts into itself."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c336cb61-bbeb-43c2-a7f6-1781d10181e5",
                                "sense_id": "42d30915-2fd0-30a6-ae46-0e65d9260863",
                                "text": "Extend the sides of triangle QRS and construct the three excircles: One excircle is tangent to side QR and rays SQ and SR; one excircle is tangent to side SR and rays QS and QR; and one excircle is tangent to side SQ and rays RS and RQ."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4f1ced0c-c21e-461b-b07f-9347d38e38a5",
                                "sense_id": "42d30915-2fd0-30a6-ae46-0e65d9260863",
                                "text": "Lemma 4.9 (The Diameter of the Incircle). Let ABC be a triangle whose incircle is tangent to #92;overline#123;BC#125; at D. If #92;overline#123;DE#125; is a diameter of the incircle and ray AE meets #92;overline#123;BC#125; at X, then BD#61;CX and X is the tangency point of the A-excircle to #92;overline#123;BC#125;.\nIncircles and excircles often have dual properties."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
